    "result": "I implemented `parse_line(line, sep=\",\")` in `solution.py`, keeping the given signature, and changed no other file. It first checks types (`TypeError`) and that `sep` is one character other than `\"`, `\\r` or `\\n` (`ValueError`). It then scans left to right: a field starting with `\"` is read as a quoted field, where `\"\"` becomes one quote and separators and newlines are ordinary characters, and the closing quote must be followed by `sep` or end of line. Otherwise the field runs to the next `sep`, and a `\"`, `\\r` or `\\n` inside it raises `ValueError`. Each separator starts a new field, so `\"\"` gives `[\"\"]`, `\"a,\"` gives `[\"a\", \"\"]`, and whitespace is never trimmed. As instructed, I did not run or test the code.",
